{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/519097-ooc-mistwatch-werewolf-the-apocalypse","id":519097,"title":"[OOC] Mistwatch - Werewolf: The Apocalypse","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play","Play by Post"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-19T01:41:01-07:00","id":519097,"title":"[OOC] Mistwatch - Werewolf: The Apocalypse","content":"Hi guys, I've thrown together some setting information, at the google docs link below. It's lengthy, but I hope it's mildly interesting/entertaining, and should give you a good idea of what to expect. Or not to expect. Use your characters from the Delaware Valley chronicle if you like, tweak them, discard them, whatever. All characters will start off as new arrivals to Mistwatch Sept, and while they'll have already undergone their rite of passage, they'll still have much to prove. If you guys could paste you character sheets into this thread, I'd appreciate it. Even if you want to completely re-do your character, we'll be using the character sheet format Jim provided, as it's pretty darn good.<br /> <br /> That should be enough to get started. Questions and suggestions are most welcome.<br /> <br /> Link to Google Doc:<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1J1n7E8QZg4jrqh6jZRNRej_K30YUZfceQpVcXp4o8vA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">https://docs.google.com/document/d/1...it?usp=sharing</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Right, so here's the character sheet template we'll be using (btw, I ripped it off someone): <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <u>Player:</u> [Screen Name is sufficient, but feel free to put your first name if you care to share. I\u2019m Josh.]<br /> <u>Chronicle:</u> Mistwatch<br /> <br /> <u>Breed:</u><br /> <u>Auspice:</u><br /> <u>Tribe:</u><br /> <u>Camp:</u> [If any]<br /> <u>Sept:</u><br /> <u>Pack Name:</u> [Leave blank for now]<br /> <u>Pack Totem:</u> [Leave blank for now]<br /> <br /> <u>Nature:</u><br /> <u>Demeanor:</u><br /> <u>Concept:</u> [Optional]<br /> <br /> <u>Attributes</u><br /> Strength: [Record attributes and abilities with a numeral, not a series of dots]<br /> Dexterity: [If there is a specialty, include it after the relevant numeral in parentheses]<br /> Stamina:<br /> <br /> Charisma:<br /> Manipulation:<br /> Appearance:<br /> <br /> Perception:<br /> Intelligence:<br /> Wits:<br /> <br /> <u>Abilities</u> [Feel free to add Hobbies/Professional Skills/Expert Knowledges to each category.]<br /> <u>Talents</u><br /> Alertness:<br /> Athletics:<br /> Brawl:<br /> Empathy:<br /> Expression:<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Leadership:<br /> Primal-Urge:<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> <u>Skills</u><br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive:<br /> Etiquette:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee:<br /> Performance:<br /> Stealth:<br /> Survival:<br /> <br /> <u>Knowledges</u><br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Enigmas:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Law:<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult:<br /> Rituals:<br /> Science:<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> <u>Backgrounds</u> [Just names and numbers here; details go below.]<br /> _____:<br /> _____:<br /> Totem:<br /> <br /> <u>Gifts</u><br /> Name (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Name (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Rites</u><br /> Name (Type; Level X; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Metis Deformity:</u> [If not Metis, please write \u201cN/A\u201d]<br /> <br /> <u>Rage:</u> X (X) [Permanent, then temporary in parentheses, which will be the same at the start]<br /> <u>Gnosis:</u> X (X)<br /> <u>Willpower:</u> X (X)<br /> <br /> <u>Renown</u><br /> <u>Glory</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Honor</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Wisdom</u><br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> <u>Rank:</u> 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u>Merits</u><br /> Name (Type; Level; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Flaws</u><br /> Name (Type; Level; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> <u>Background Descriptions</u><br /> [Any background that requires an explanation, such as the identity of an Ally or the nature of a Fetish, should have a listing here.]<br /> <br /> <u>Age:</u><br /> <u>Apparent Age:</u> [For Metis and Lupus, it will be the age your homid form appears.]<br /> <u>Sign:</u> [For Garou Astrology. If you\u2019re unfamiliar, leave blank for now.]<br /> <u>Race:</u> [Racial phenotype of the character\u2019s homid form. Use whatever descriptor you like.]<br /> <u>Sex:</u> [By which I mean their anatomy]<br /> <u>Gender:</u> [Use whatever descriptor you like, or leave blank if you prefer]<br /> <u>Sexuality:</u> [Use whatever descriptor you like, or leave blank if you prefer]<br /> <u>Hair Color:</u><br /> <u>Fur Color:</u> [Obviously this applies to Crinos, Hispo and Lupus forms]<br /> <u>Eye Color:</u><br /> <u>Height:</u> [Homid form]<br /> <u>Weight:</u> [Homid form]<br /> <u>Build:</u> [Whatever descriptor you like, just a one or two word blurb to help us envision.]<br /> <u>Distinctive Features:</u> [Any particular features useful in identifying your character, be they visual, auditory or olfactory.]<br /> <br /> <u>Appearance</u><br /> [Give a general description of your character\u2019s appearance in Homid, Crinos and Lupus forms. If you\u2019re feeling especially industrious, you can do so for Glabro and Hispo as well. For homid form, include a brief description of the clothing that the character is most often wearing.]<br /> <br /> <u>Equipment</u><br /> [Any particular or distinctive equipment that your character owns that you want to record. The make, model and color of her car, for example, or her heirloom pocket watch. Bear in mind the resources rating and be reasonable. Remember, this is not D&amp;D- not every piece of equipment needs to be accounted for. Unless you really, REALLY want to be sure your character has that 10 foot pole and 50 ft of hemp rope.]<br /> <br /> <u>Personality</u><br /> [Just a few sentences of summation of what the character is like, on the level of personal interactions. If you were this character\u2019s friend, and had to describe what she is like to someone who had never met her, what would you say?]<br /> <br /> <u>Character History</u><br /> [The character\u2019s history and backstory, in your own words. Most of this will be what we discussed in the recruitment thread, but here is the chance to fill in some blanks and put it all in one place, for easier reference for all of us.]<br /> <br /> <u>Notes</u><br /> [Any notes you want to jot down about your character to have readily available for easy reference. Names of family members living or dead, particular goals, aspirations or fears, etc.]<br /> <br /> <u>Renown Details</u><br /> [This space is for me to record the details of any renown won (or lost) by your character, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> <u>Experience</u><br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> A few other notes: <br /> <br /> - No Rite of Talisman Dedication. In this crazy alternate universe, werewolves don't shred their clothing when they shift. Trust me, it's better this way. <br /> - No super-powered Fetishes or Talens. This goes without saying. <br /> - Everyone takes at least one point in the Totem background. The pack will be stuck together for a while, and this will represent this. Remember, the more points in Totem, the more powerful it'll be. You guys will get to choose your totem as the game goes on. <br /> - No Fate background.<br /> - And no Dark Fate flaw. <br /> - Silver Fangs must have a minimum of 3 in Pure Breed.<br /> - Gnosis and Willpower may not be raised higher than 8 at character creation. No exceptions. Rage can be as high as you wish...<br /> <br /> Attributes will use the standard 7/5/3 split. Ratings of 1 or 5 will require some sort of exceptional explanation. Also, choose a specialization for every attribute rated 4 and above. Custom one's welcome. <br /> <br /> As for abilities, it's the regular 13/9/5 spread. However, there should be something in your character's background to justify all their abilities to some extent. Ratings of 5 in anything will be severely scrutinized. Kailindo, Klaiveskar, Iksakku are off-limits, even if your mentor happens to be an elder Stargazer (ahem). All lupus characters must take at least one dot in Primal Urge to represent their lupine instincts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 05-26-2015, 09:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T11:46:47-07:00","id":519815,"title":"","content":"Your setting is super unrealistic. Val as a wise and respected Ragabash? Come on. Write something more believable.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-19T19:58:24-07:00","id":520371,"title":"","content":"Shhh. The setting materials all written by him, so the perspective might be <i>slightly</i> skewed. I guess I got a bit attached to the character and wanted to do something with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T10:57:25-07:00","id":528980,"title":"","content":"Man, I'm really uninspired for a character... I guess I'll rework Geoff, but I'm having trouble coming up with interesting twists for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;And for my next trick&quot; I said, &quot;anvils!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2016-evilmarmelade","name":"Evilmarmelade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2016_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"632"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-26T18:17:24-07:00","id":529471,"title":"","content":"Did you read through all the setting stuff? Was there nothing there that looked like a plot hook? I'm happy to help you come up with ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-06T11:01:37-07:00","id":542750,"title":"","content":"Sorry for taking so long, been really busy. Life can be a bitch that way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b><u>Player:</u></b> Vidyaraja (Alessandro)<br /> <b><u>Chronicle:</u></b> Mistwatch<br /> <br /> <b><u>Breed:</u></b> Lupus<br /> <u><b>Auspice:</b></u> Ahroun<br /> <u><b>Tribe:</b></u> Silver Fangs<br /> <u><b>House:</b></u> Wyrmfoe<br /> <u><b>Lodge:</b></u> Lodge of the Moon<br /> <u><b>Sept:</b></u> Mistwatch<br /> <u><b>Pack Name:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Pack Totem:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Nature:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Demeanor:</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Attributes</b></u><br /> <u>Strength:</u> 3<br /> <u>Dexterity:</u> 4<br /> <u>Stamina:</u> 3<br /> <br /> <u>Charisma:</u> 3<br /> <u>Manipulation:</u> 1<br /> <u>Appearance:</u> 2<br /> <br /> <u>Perception:</u> 3<br /> <u>Intelligence:</u> 2<br /> <u>Wits:</u> 3<br /> <br /> <u><b>Talents</b></u><br /> <u>Alertness:</u> 3<br /> <u>Athletics:</u> 3<br /> <u>Brawl:</u> 4<br /> Empathy:<br /> Expression:<br /> <u>Intimidation:</u> 1<br /> Leadership:<br /> <u>Primal-Urge:</u> 3<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Skills</b></u><br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive:<br /> Etiquette:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> <u>Melee:</u> 2<br /> <u>Performance:</u> 1<br /> <u>Stealth:</u> 3<br /> <u>Survival:</u> 3<br /> <br /> Knowledges<br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> <u>Enigmas:</u> 1<br /> Investigation:<br /> Law:<br /> <u>Medicine:</u> 2<br /> Occult:<br /> <u>Rituals:</u> 2<br /> Science:<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> <u><b>Backgrounds </b></u><br /> <u>Rites:</u> 2<br /> <u>Pure Breed:</u> 3<br /> <u>Totem:</u> 3<br /> <u>Contacts:</u> 2<br /> <br /> <u><b>Gifts</b></u><br /> Heightened Senses (Lupus, Level 1, W20-158)<br /> Falling Touch (Ahroun, Level 1, W20-171)<br /> Sense Wyrm (Silver Fangs, Level 1, W20-156)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rites</b></u><br /> Rite of Binding (Mystic, Level 1, W20-210)<br /> Prayer for the Prey, Greet the Moon (Minor, W20-220)<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Rage:</b></u> 6 (6)<br /> <u><b>Gnosis:</b></u> 6 (6)<br /> <u><b>Willpower:</b></u> 6 (6)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Renown</b></u><br /> <u><b>Glory</b></u><br /> <u>Permanent:</u> 3<br /> <u>Temporary:</u> 0<br /> <br /> <u><b>Honor</b></u><br /> <u>Permanent:</u> 0<br /> <u>Temporary:</u> 0<br /> <br /> <u><b>Wisdom</b></u><br /> <u>Permanent:</u> 0<br /> <u>Temporary:</u> 0<br /> <br /> <u><b>Rank:</b></u> 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Background Descriptions</b></u><br /> <u>Pure Breed :</u> Many generations removed from his lineage, Shine Talon is still a Silver Fang, though some say &quot;barely&quot;<br /> <u>Rites :</u> His traidtionalist tribe wouldn't teach him the Rite of Binding; he bargained with the Talons for tutelage in this Mystic Rite<br /> <u>Totem :</u> Shine Talon has a good relationship with the natural world and spirits, so he naturally will have a deep connection to whatever totem adopts his pack<br /> <u>Contacts:</u> An extended network of acquaitances and friends of convenience among the Red Talons<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><b>Age:</b></u> 30 months (give or take)<br /> <u><b>Apparent Age:</b></u> 20-25<br /> <u><b>Sign:</b></u><br /> <u><b>Race:</b></u> Caucasian<br /> <u><b>Sex:</b></u> Male<br /> <u><b>Sexuality:</b></u> Heterosexual, not really interested in humans of either gender<br /> <u><b>Hair Color:</b></u> Dirt blonde<br /> <u><b>Fur Color:</b></u> A dirty, grayish white<br /> <u><b>Eye Color:</b></u> Brown<br /> <u><b>Height:</b></u> 177 cms<br /> <u><b>Weight:</b></u> 77 kgs<br /> <u><b>Build:</b></u> Well-developed muscles, strong and athletic<br /> <u><b>Distinctive Features:</b></u> In lupine forms his claws are of the purest white<br /> <br /> <u><b>Appearance</b></u><br /> <u>Homid:</u> Tall and muscular, would be cute but he scowls semi-permanently; only truly smiles at things he intends to hurt. Dresses in hand-me-downs, usually rips his clothes in places where they are too small for him.<br /> <u>Lupus:</u> More white overall than your typical timber wolf; big, strong and mean-looking. Unusually colored nails that give him his deed name.<br /> <u>Crinos:</u> His fur shifts more towards pure white in this form. His white talons also become really apparent here.<br /> (As a side note, Werewolf art tends to show Garou with white claws, though wolves, even arctic woles, tend to have dark claws)<br /> <br /> <u><b>Equipment</b></u><br /> None, thouhg at any given time he might have stashes of talens he bargained for or bound himself hiddne in various parts of his home range<br /> <br /> <u><b>Personality</b></u><br /> Seems aloof and distant at first, but he just tends to put on a show to people he doesn't know. In reality he's quite friendly to people / wolves he gets to know, though he doesn't show that well in human shapes. Calm, analytical and patient, he nonetheless tends to snap even at friends if he doesn't get some time alone for self-reflection now and then. Values instinct over human-think and he's brutally honest because he chose to discard the concept of &quot;tact&quot; his tribemates tried to teach him. Overall people who know him well find that as long as they respect his boundaries he's friendly and loyal.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Character History</b></u><br /> When the Fangs first came to the area around Mistwatch, a single lupus among them tried to claim a strong pack of wolves as his Kinfolk. After watching four generations of his descendants in which not even a single pup bred true, he left in search of better stock and the lineage became a footnote in the Homid-written history of the local Fangs.<br /> Now, more than a century later, his efforts finally bore fruit. Though dozens of generations removed and unnoticed by a long-dormant Kin-Fetch spirit, a pup was not only bred true, but with enough lingering purity of blood that Falcon would not disdain him.<br /> Shine Talon's life was pretty unremarkable for a wolf pup until his First Change. He played and hunted with his brothers, quickly outdoing them in both cunning and strength. When their father became too old to lead and hunt and it was time to make a play for dominance, though, things turned bloody. As he was holding down his struggling brother, the Change came on him. He tore the wolf from piece to piece, and the rest of the pack scattered, never to come together again.<br /> The Talons found the young werewolf, wailing in a furless guise, overcome by emotions and understanding neither. They estabilished he was of their breed, but their spirits also showed them that he was not of theirs and they should contact the Silver Fangs.<br /> The Fangs didn't really know what to make of the pup. They managed to identify his lineage, but his closest relatives dwelled in woods hundreds of miles away. Besides they had no heirloom, no title, no nothing to offer to a scion so far removed. So it wsa that Shine Talon stayed here in Mistwatch, he underwent tutelage by a Homid warrior and took his Rite of Passage with cubs from other tribes.<br /> Nowadays the Fangs stationed him in Mistwatch because they don't trust him enough to keep him close but they don't trust him enough to let him roam free either. They taught him enough human get-by to not threaten the Veil then happily discharged the responsibility to Ragnar and his septmates. As for Shine Talon, he feels more kinship with wolves and the Red Talon tribe than with homids; he frequently visits his home range and trades favors and tutelage with the Talons of the Devourer.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Renown Details</b></u><br /> <br /> <u><b>Experience</b></u><br /> <u><b>Saved:</b></u> 0<br /> <u><b>Spent:</b></u> 0<br /> <u><b>Total:</b></u> 0</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Some details are missing, like Nature and Demeanor and Specialties and maybe I'll take some Flaws. But otherwise this is pretty much how it's going to be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-12T23:50:56-07:00","id":552614,"title":"","content":"Great stuff Alessandro. I too have been rather busy, which explains my absence. Although no one else seems to have stopped by...Hmm...<br /> <br /> Anyway, I have a few questions about Shine Talon: <br /> <br /> 1. You mention a 'Lodge', is this something from <i>Werewolf: The Forsaken</i>? I've never encountered it before. Is it just another word for 'camp'?<br /> <br /> 2. Shine Talon has a lot of contacts. Are you okay with me making them up, or is there a specific contact you wanted me to include in the story? <br /> <br /> 3. Who was the 'homid warrior' who taught Shine Talon to fight? That seems like a pretty big deal. Does Shine Talon still have contact with this person? They can be someone important from the sept if you like. Ariadne would be a good choice. <br /> <br /> 4. The way you've written the character history implies Talon (can I call him that?) is bound to Mistwatch. I'm okay with this, but he WILL get manipulated, and not just by Ragnar. If you're fine with this possibility, let me know. <br /> <br /> 5. The Sept of the Devourer aren't fans of Mistwatch. Do they know Talon is attached to the sept? <br /> <br /> 6. Talon's original pack scattered when he underwent the First Change. Does he want to find them and reconnect? <br /> <br /> <br /> I'll let you handle nature and demeanor, (Loner might be a good choice though) although if you want to come up with custom ones, feel free, just check with me first. If you're intent on a Flaw, maybe Insane Ancestor? The Silver Fang lupus who wanted to produce garou offspring might have taken notice of Talon. He has fulfilled his dream after all, and perhaps this ancestor isn't pleased with the direction Talon has taken? Finally, if you're not versed in Garou astrology, here's a list and description of all the star signs: <a href=\"http://darkshadows.awardspace.com/shifters/calendar.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkshadows.awardspace.com/shifters/calendar.htm</a> I apologize for the terrible font and late-90s site layout, but it's the best one I could find (which is saying something.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T04:10:18-07:00","id":554132,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I thought at first thet I wanted to wait to see someone else's work before I posted mine, but of course if everyone thought like this we'd never go anywhere. So I did hte opposite and hope that seeing us working on my PC will inspire someone else to post.<br /> <br /> Anyway, on to your questions:<br /> <br /> 1 - Lodges are mentioned in both Silver Fangs tribebook and, I believe, in W20. It's a SF thing where each one of htem is encouraged to choose either the Lodge of the Sun or the Moon, which are kind of administrative bureaus with ritualistic overtones. The Lodge of the Sun is concerned with worldly matters, politics and the human population; the Lodge of the Moon with wilderness, the spirit world and wolves. A proper SF court is attended by at least a steward, shaman and squire from each Lodge, plus a seneschal from one or the other. They also have some Gifts like Camps do, but overall it's just a bit of flavor you can ignore if the story isn't that SF-centric.<br /> <br /> 2 - Feel free to make my major Contacts up. I wouldn't know what REd Talons NPCs would work best in your setting.<br /> <br /> 3 - I thought of that person as just some guy who wanted to score some quick and dirty Honor for mentoring then went their own way as soon as they did the bare minimum. That's why I didn't purchase Mentor. Even if we make it one of your named NPCs I don't relay think they'd have more than a casual, cordial relationship.<br /> <br /> 4 - Well, they can try! Of course a homid could be tricked into thinking Talon is too dense to be useful even if successfully manipulated. (He's not stupid at all, he just thinks very differently and values very different things from the homid around him.)<br /> <br /> 5 - I imagine they knew, and there would be some things he wouldn't be trusted with, but overall the relationship keeps working. Unless that doesn't work for your story in which case I'd have to tweak my backstory a bit.<br /> <br /> 6 - They were so terrified by the experience that they all started living as lone wolves and keep on doing so. Talon feels a lot of guilt over this, but he figures at least he can respect their wishes, watch them from afar and protect them when he can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-23T13:34:51-07:00","id":565714,"title":"","content":"So, no one interested anymore I guess?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-24T19:25:59-07:00","id":567251,"title":"","content":"Duuude...I can't believe it. I mean I had like 6 people who said they were down for it. I have no idea what happened. I know I've been AWOL, but I didn't suspect I would come back to...this. It's kinda disappointing. I guess I'll leave things open for now, but there's no point running the game with one player, sorry Alessandro.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-25T06:14:25-07:00","id":567797,"title":"","content":"Eeeeh, I confess to having left hanging my share of online games, myself. It's just something that sometimes happens when there's no direct social contact involved.<br /> Nest time, then!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-26T07:21:58-07:00","id":569180,"title":"","content":"Ah... sorry for disappearing. Again. I had my sheet finished, but life's been throwing a lot of problems my way the past two months. &gt;_&lt; Would two players be enough to keep this alive?<br /> <br /> The character was Stir of Echoes, reimagined as a Ragabash Red Talon.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T00:05:27-07:00","id":570012,"title":"","content":"That's cool Eve, you're here now. Let's see if I can drag someone else in first. Bashir also seemed quite interested, but I think he's got stuff to deal with at the moment. I just didn't want to start the game, then have people arrive late, but what the hell, I'll improvise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T09:07:15-07:00","id":570286,"title":"","content":"I see. I hope he's doing well.<br /> <br /> I do have a friend who might be interested. I'll poke them and see if he'll come around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:37:06-07:00","id":570332,"title":"","content":"And here I am. I don't really know the game, but I'm interested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6642-abhimanyu","name":"Abhimanyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-27T10:42:24-07:00","id":570334,"title":"","content":"We'll turn you into a proper nerd soon enough. ;D","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-01T18:52:07-07:00","id":575897,"title":"","content":"Great...Although I hope Alessandro hasn't wandered off...Also, I've just realized I've been away for a week. Not a good example. I'll make sure to check this thread once a day. So, Abhimanyu, when you say you don't really know the game, how much of it are you familiar with? The background? The tribes you can play as?<br /> <br /> PS: Also, with a name screen name like Abhimanyu, I'm guessing you're into Indian mythology? This bodes well...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3869,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","user":"Al-Haleem","date":". 07-01-2015, 09:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-02T11:00:05-07:00","id":576615,"title":"","content":"Eve explained the basics of the game to me. What interested me the most was a Homid/Ahroun/Glass Walker. Born in India, came over to the USA to study engineering and then had his first change. And yeah, I used to watch Mahabharatha when I was a kid in Kerala. <br /> <br /> I noticed the Narasimha avatar. You wouldn't happen to be Indian, if I may ask?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6642-abhimanyu","name":"Abhimanyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-03T02:40:15-07:00","id":577179,"title":"","content":"Right. Have any idea what this character's name is? Did you read the background info in the first post? How would your character fit in amongst the Garou of San Francisco? What does he want to get out of his new life? <br /> <br /> And I'm half Indian, on my mom's side. Werewolf the Apocalypse is woefully lacking in Indian stuff, so I work as much of it in as I can, glad there's a chance of someone getting all the references now : p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-04T22:35:11-07:00","id":579483,"title":"","content":"Just posting to let people know I'm still alive. :-D Holiday weekend ate up my time, but I should have her sheet (found a few things I wanted to work out) posted within the next few days.<br /> <br /> I've talked to Abhi, too, and he'll have his full concept ready soon as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T02:14:42-07:00","id":579652,"title":"","content":"Thanks for keeping me informed Eve, and I'm glad Abhi's got a handle on stuff, looking forward to seeing his character concept. No clue what happened to the other dude, hopefully he'll check back, if not, eh, I can wing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T13:33:25-07:00","id":580133,"title":"","content":"I am still here, yeah, lurking and waiting. And thinking about Merits &amp; Flaws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:49:59-07:00","id":580473,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's her sheet. She's... very specialized, but I hope that's okay. Still have a few things left to do, mainly the personality and background, which I wanted to ask about before I started writing it.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Player:</b> Eve<br /> <b>Chronicle:</b> Mistwatch<br /> <br /> <b>Breed:</b> Lupus<br /> <b>Auspice:</b> Ragabash<br /> <b>Tribe:</b> Red Talon<br /> <b>Camp:</b><br /> <b>Sept:</b> Mistwatch<br /> <b>Pack Name:</b> [Leave blank for now]<br /> <b>Pack Totem</b>: [Leave blank for now]<br /> <br /> <b>Nature:<br /> Demeanor:<br /> Concept</b>: [Optional]<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> <b>Strength:</b> 3<br /> <b>Dexterity</b>: 3<br /> <b>Stamina:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Charisma</b>: 2<br /> <b>Manipulation</b>: 2<br /> <b>Appearance:</b> 2<br /> <br /> <b>Perception:</b> 4 [Uncanny Instincts]<br /> <b>Intelligence: </b>2<br /> <b>Wits</b>: 4 [Cool-Headed]<br /> <br /> Abilities<br /> Talents<br /> Alertness: 4 [Ambushes]<br /> Athletics: 3<br /> Brawl: 3<br /> Empathy:<br /> Expression:<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Leadership:<br /> Primal-Urge: 3<br /> Streetwise:<br /> Subterfuge:<br /> <br /> Skills<br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts:<br /> Drive:<br /> Etiquette:<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee:<br /> Performance: 1<br /> Stealth: 4 [Shadowing]<br /> Survival: 4 [Tracking]<br /> <br /> Knowledges<br /> Academics:<br /> Computer:<br /> Enigmas: 2<br /> Investigation: 2<br /> Law:<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult: 2<br /> Rituals:<br /> Science:<br /> Technology:<br /> <br /> Backgrounds [Just names and numbers here; details go below.]<br /> Ancestors: 5<br /> Pure Breed: 1<br /> Totem: 2<br /> Mentor: 4<br /> <br /> Gifts<br /> Blur of the Milky Eye (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Heightened Senses (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> Hidden Killer (Breed/Auspice/Tribe; Level 1; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> Name (Type; Level X; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> Metis Deformity: N/A<br /> <br /> Rage: 2 (2) [Permanent, then temporary in parentheses, which will be the same at the start]<br /> Gnosis: 5 (X)<br /> Willpower: 3 (3)<br /> <br /> Renown<br /> Glory<br /> Permanent: 2<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Honor<br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Wisdom<br /> Permanent: 1<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Rank: 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Homid Ancestor (Social/Spiritual; 2; Red Talons Revised, pg.78)<br /> Wolf Sight (Physical, 1; W20 pg.472)<br /> Acute Sense - Hearing (Physical; 1; W20 pg.472)<br /> Acute Sense - Sight (Physical; 1; W20 pg.472)<br /> Acute Sense - Scent (Physical; 1; W20 pg.472)<br /> Untamable (Mental; 5; W20 pg.476)<br /> <br /> Flaws<br /> Sign of the Wolf (Supernatural; 2; W20 pg.484)<br /> Strict Carnivore (Physical; 1; W20 pg.473)<br /> Pack Mentality (Mental; 2; W20 pg.477)<br /> Mark of the Predator (Supernatural; 2; W20 pg.484)<br /> <br /> Background Descriptions<br /> Perception, Wits, Alertness, Survival, Stealth<br /> Forced to fend for herself from a young age, Echo has been honing these skills ever since. Without them, she would've never survived the worlds of both man and wolf. After her Change, the Talons noted her talent, and honed them even further, very intent on making her the &quot;sneak and murder&quot; type of Ragabash, over the stereotypical trickster.<br /> <br /> Wolf Sight, Acute Senses<br /> For long as she can remember, she's been sensitive to the slightest movements, sound and smells; perhaps this is another reason why she put so much work into her sensory skills, to obtain some sense of control against the overwhelming stimuli of daily life.<br /> <br /> Untamable, Pack Mentality<br /> Try as they might, Echo refused to be leashed by any man, and has proved resistant against mind controlling gifts (much to the chagrin of her superiors.) Her soul is wild, through and through.<br /> <br /> At the same time, she is lost without her pack. Alone, she is nervous, prone to making mistakes.<br /> <br /> Sign of the Wolf, Mark of the Wolf, Strict Carnivore<br /> If you asked some random citizen to point out a werewolf, they'd probably point to Echo. Animals shy away from her. She's hairy, her eyes appear almost yellow and her palms just happen to have lines that look like a pentagram. Oh, and she only eats meat. Anything else makes her ill.<br /> <br /> Homid Ancestor, Ancestors<br /> A dark secret. Nobody, not even Echo herself knows that there is a homid in her ancestral tree. Her mother, or father, was Garou, and they certainly weren't Red Talons. Dreams and memories of both wolf and human plague her. She leaves out the human part when talking to tribe mates.<br /> <br /> They likely wouldn't be forgiving if they knew the truth.<br /> <br /> Mentor<br /> <br /> Age: 2<br /> Apparent Age: 15<br /> Sign: Rorg<br /> Race: White<br /> Sex: Female<br /> Gender: Female<br /> Sexuality: Unknown<br /> Hair Color: Reddish<br /> Fur Color: Reddish<br /> Eye Color: Dull green, gold specks<br /> Height: 5'1<br /> Weight: 124 lbs<br /> Build: Wiry, lean; more muscle than fat.<br /> Distinctive Features: Wild, unkempt hair; &quot;Signs of the Wolf&quot;.<br /> <br /> Appearance<br /> Homid<br /> Echo could be the poster girl for feral children, with her dirty skin, her animalistic gait, and her wide, round eyes that always appear to be on the alert, and which, on occasion, seem more yellow than green. She's pale, very pale, and quite short as well, made more apparent by the slouch in her shoulders - it's clear she's uncomfortable in this 'skin.' Her hair doesn't fall below the ear, and looks as though it's been cut with a rusty knife or sharp rock, with strands of various different lengths. It's a sort of dark coppery blonde in color, or auburn, and always tangled, never brushed. Physically speaking, she's scrawny, but tough, with what muscles she has readily apparent, lithe and limber.<br /> <br /> She's not a fan of clothes, and, unless absolutely necessary, she doesn't wear them, preferring instead to wander nude (in breed form). If the situation calls for them, she grabs whatever's available, without regard to style or good fashion sense. Her choices tend to be very bland (or very garish, if you let go wild), very &quot;blue collar&quot;, and often a size too big. She can't stand long sleeves, or collars that reach around the neck.<br /> <br /> Lupus<br /> Here is where she truly excels, moving with a predatory grace few outside the Talon's can match. Powerful muscles ripple under thick red fur, fur that's painted with black patterns that run down from the nape of her neck to the tip of her tail. In stark contrast, below the jaw, the stomach and the legs are white. Her eyes a bright, intense gold.<br /> <br /> Crinos<br /> She bears the visage of the penultimate hunter, a towering mass of muscle and sinew. Each limb is of equal width, made more for the chase and a quick, brutal kill over prolonged fighting. The red-black patterns of her fur have merged to become a dark, almost maroon shade, with one exception: at her knees and elbows, the color fades into a milky white, creating 'socks'. Her eyes are a brilliant gold, and they always seem to catch light in such a way that causes her pupils to 'glow.'<br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> Zilch.<br /> <br /> Personality<br /> To sum her up in one word? Quiet. She's a wolf lost in thought, trying to make sense of all this madness. This might make her come off as aloof or cold, but beneath all that is a passionate woman, struggling to reign in her emotions. This passion leads to strong opinions, and Echo's not one to hold her tongue when the pressure's on; if you've been acting the fool and ask for her opinion, she'll lay it out bluntly, explaining why you're a moron (and what you ought to do to fix that). This is not meant to insult (well, usually), but to help, as Echo grows attached easily, and only wants to see that her people remain safe.<br /> <br /> Part of this is born out of insecurity. Echo fears losing someone again, and she's found that, if they don't respect wisdom, they certainly do respect fear. There's a darker side to this - she'll deny it viciously, but deep down, she gets a morbid sense of pleasure and comfort from seeing others recoil from her presence.<br /> <br /> Character History<br /> [The character\u2019s history and backstory, in your own words. Most of this will be what we discussed in the recruitment thread, but here is the chance to fill in some blanks and put it all in one place, for easier reference for all of us.]<br /> <br /> Notes<br /> [Any notes you want to jot down about your character to have readily available for easy reference. Names of family members living or dead, particular goals, aspirations or fears, etc.]<br /> <br /> Renown Details<br /> [This space is for me to record the details of any renown won (or lost) by your character, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> Experience<br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> <br /> flaw +7 = 22 freebie points<br /> -2, -1, -3 merits<br /> -1 ancestors 5<br /> -2 totem 2<br /> -1 for pure breed<br /> -5 for untamable<br /> -4 for mentor 4<br /> -2 for willpower 3<br /> -1 for rage 2</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The gist of what I had in mind for her history is this:<br /> <br /> One of her parents (or grandparents) is garou, a homid that may still be in or near Mistwatch. Nobody, except for maybe a select few, know this. All that Echo knows is that she is plagued by weird dreams/ancestral memories, and that when she was a pup she was sold to a guy in the city. The idiot wasn't prepared to take care of a wild animal, so after a few months of home destruction, he dumped her on the streets, where she scraped by until she stumbled across Muir Woods, and the Talons took her in. Well, actually, there was squabbling between the Gnawers and Talons for her, but the Talons won. She is, after all, their kin, even if the blood is thin.<br /> <br /> After she changed, they worked on making her the perfect killer.<br /> <br /> And that's what I've got so far. I'm not sure why they'd send her to Mistwatch. Maybe to spy? Echo would want to leave, if only to figure out what happened to her. And to find a pack that wouldn't look down on her for her city origins.<br /> <br /> That also brings me to my next question: would Val be available as a Mentor? I don't know how or why that would happen, yet, but it could be part of the reason she came to the sept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-11T02:02:00-07:00","id":586924,"title":"","content":"Righto. I can see what you mean about specialized, which isn't <i>too </i>much of a problem. Alessandro wants to play a combat type character, and Abhi also wants to be an Ahroun (May I suggest a Philodox for balance reasons?) I'm glad you picked up on the Talons hatred of Mistwatch, and them sending Echo to spy makes sense, especially as she's a 'city wolf' and thus would blend in better. Also, most Talons would loathe the idea of spending extended periods in San Francisco, so Echo makes a good lackey. However, if she's a 'perfect killer' she might not be the most effective spy. Assassin maybe? And Val could indeed be a mentor, although he won't be very reliable. As for why he chose to mentor her...he moves in mysterious ways. Possibly he knows her homid ancestor. Maybe he approached Echo when she arrived, presenting himself as a friend and ally. And Echo would need all the allies she could get, after all, she's in enemy territory. If you want to link him with Echo's reason for coming to the sept, maybe the Talons believe Val can be turned against Ragnar, and thus weaken Mistwatch. Just an idea. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-13T12:04:08-07:00","id":589454,"title":"","content":"To be honest my concept doesn't revolve that much around an Auspice, so I can play a Philodox or whatever is needed, if you'd rather have a different Auspice for every player.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-15T01:05:34-07:00","id":591014,"title":"","content":"Only if you want to. But going by Talon's desire to network with his fellow garou and keep things civil, he does seem to have the balanced mindset a good philodox would have. It's not imperative, but seeing as we only have three players (so far) having everyone be a different auspice allows for more roleplaying opportunities (and helps me create specific content for each player). Hopefully I'll get a glimpse of Abhi's character sheet soon. Remember guys, the sooner you complete them, the sooner we can start playing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-16T08:04:15-07:00","id":592631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Al-Haleem</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/519097-ooc-mistwatch-werewolf-the-apocalypse?p=586924#post586924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, if she's a 'perfect killer' she might not be the most effective spy. Assassin maybe? And Val could indeed be a mentor, although he won't be very reliable. As for why he chose to mentor her...he moves in mysterious ways. Possibly he knows her homid ancestor. Maybe he approached Echo when she arrived, presenting himself as a friend and ally. And Echo would need all the allies she could get, after all, she's in enemy territory. If you want to link him with Echo's reason for coming to the sept, maybe the Talons believe Val can be turned against Ragnar, and thus weaken Mistwatch. Just an idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds good to me. They send her to keep tabs on things, and to see if Val can be swayed to their cause. They could also try to spin a story around her arrival, claiming that it's an act of goodwill that they're handing over one of their few, precious pups. Surely, if they had insidious intentions, they would not be risking her life.<br /> <br /> Not likely that anyone would believe that, but it's a cover story.<br /> <br /> <b>News from Abhi:</b> he should have his app up by tomorrow night. He's sorry for the delay, but he's been incredibly busy, being his last month in grad school and all. He's also cool with going Philodox.<br /> <br /> Although, with two Ahrouns and a Red Talon, we'd have the market cornered on murdering things.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><u>Rage Across the Delaware Valley</u><br /> <b>Health: </b><br /> <b>Rage (3)</b>:<br /> <b>Gnosis (7):</b> X<br /> <b>Willpower (6): </b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3804-stir-of-echoes","name":"Stir of Echoes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"79"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T12:31:02-07:00","id":594055,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay. I was a bit busy with college. <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Player: Abhi<br /> Chronicle: Mistwatch<br /> <br /> Breed: Homid<br /> Auspice: Philodox<br /> Tribe: Glass Walkers<br /> Camp: Random Interrupts/Cyber Dogs*<br /> Sept: Mistwatch<br /> Pack Name: [Leave blank for now]<br /> Pack Totem: [Leave blank for now]<br /> <br /> Nature: Survivor<br /> Demeanor: Judge<br /> Concept: [Optional]<br /> <br /> Attributes<br /> Strength: 2<br /> Dexterity: 2<br /> Stamina: 2<br /> <br /> Charisma: 3<br /> Manipulation: 3<br /> Appearance: 3<br /> <br /> Perception: 3<br /> Intelligence: 4<br /> Wits: 3<br /> <br /> Abilities [Feel free to add Hobbies/Professional Skills/Expert Knowledges to each category.]<br /> Talents<br /> Alertness: 1<br /> Athletics: 1<br /> Brawl: 2<br /> Empathy: 3<br /> Expression:<br /> Intimidation:<br /> Leadership: 2<br /> Primal-Urge:<br /> Streetwise: 1<br /> Subterfuge: 3<br /> <br /> Skills<br /> Animal Ken:<br /> Crafts: 2<br /> Drive:<br /> Etiquette: 1<br /> Firearms:<br /> Larceny:<br /> Melee:<br /> Performance:<br /> Stealth: 2<br /> Survival: <br /> <br /> Knowledges<br /> Academics: 2<br /> Computer: 4 [Hacking]<br /> Enigmas:<br /> Investigation:<br /> Law: 2<br /> Medicine:<br /> Occult:<br /> Rituals:<br /> Science: 2<br /> Technology: 4 [Computers]<br /> <br /> Backgrounds <br /> Resources: 4<br /> Totem: 2<br /> <br /> Gifts<br /> Persuasion (Homid; Level 1; W20 153)<br /> Truth of Gaia (Philodox; Level 1; W20 166)<br /> Plug and Play (Glass Walkers; Level 1; W20 183)<br /> <br /> Rites<br /> Name (Type; Level X; Book &amp; Page Number)<br /> <br /> Metis Deformity: N/A<br /> <br /> Rage: 3 (3) [Permanent, then temporary in parentheses, which will be the same at the start]<br /> Gnosis: 1 (1)<br /> Willpower: 3 (3)<br /> <br /> Renown<br /> Glory<br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Honor<br /> Permanent: 3<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Wisdom<br /> Permanent:<br /> Temporary:<br /> <br /> Rank: 1 (Cliath)<br /> <br /> Merits<br /> Computer Aptitude (Mental; 1; W20 474)<br /> Languages (Mental - Hindi, English; 2; W20 475)<br /> Supporter (Social; 2; W20 480)<br /> <br /> Flaws<br /> Persistant Parents (Social; 2; W20 481)<br /> Hunted (Social; 4; W20 481)<br /> <br /> Background Descriptions<br /> Persistant Parents<br /> They're rich, and he's their only child. They won't let him go so easily. <br /> <br /> Hunted<br /> One of the three people he attacked during his First Change survived. Not only that, but they remember everything. His face before he became the monster that killed their brothers. They know who he is, where he lives, and they won't stop until they've got their revenge.<br /> <br /> Random Interrupts/Cyber Dogs<br /> While not formally apart of either of these camps, they interest him the most.<br /> <br /> Age: 21<br /> Apparent Age: 21<br /> Sign: [For Garou Astrology. If you\u2019re unfamiliar, leave blank for now.]<br /> Race: Indian<br /> Sex: Male<br /> Gender: Male<br /> Sexuality: Hetero<br /> Hair Color: Black<br /> Fur Color: Black<br /> Eye Color: Brown<br /> Height: 5'10<br /> Weight: 142 lbs<br /> Build: Tall, wiry<br /> Distinctive Features: Slight accent.<br /> <br /> Appearance<br /> In homid, he's tall &amp; wiry, skinnier than most garou would like. Dark skin, dark eyes, and black hair that's begun to grow past his ears. Similarly, he's been forgetting to shave, sporting stubble over his angular face.<br /> <br /> In lupus, he's slim, even for a wolf, with shaggy black fur and yellow eyes.<br /> <br /> In crinos, he's finally got something resembling muscles, standing at almost 10 feet and dressed entirely in black (even his eyes) with long, wicked claws.<br /> <br /> Equipment<br /> Top of the line computer equipment, disposable cellphones, duffel bags to carry it all around.<br /> <br /> Personality<br /> Jovial, or, at least, he tries to hide what he's really thinking behind a grin. Incomplete.<br /> <br /> Character History<br /> Nobody knew of his garou heritage, not his mother, or father, or anyone else in his family, stretching generations back. He was a single child to a wealthy family (his birth rendering his mother infertile), their &quot;crown jewel&quot;, and they pushed him to excellence, whether he wanted it or not. When, at 19, he got the chance to leave the country, he jumped at it, flying over to San Francisco to study engineering.<br /> <br /> Life was good, for a little while. Almost a year, in fact, until one night when the First Change hit him. He killed three people before the Glass Walkers found him. That, combined with being forced into another, even more alien culture, is what drove him to run away, to try and escape back to India. He failed, of course, and got a good beating for they called cowardice. He begrudgingly accepted his fate.<br /> <br /> Later, when he earned back a little respect, he was tasked with hacking into the computers, phones, and communications of the other tribes kinfolk, hunting down blackmail material to give the Glass Walkers an upper hand in taking Mistwatch.<br /> <br /> Notes<br /> [Any notes you want to jot down about your character to have readily available for easy reference. Names of family members living or dead, particular goals, aspirations or fears, etc.]<br /> <br /> Renown Details<br /> [This space is for me to record the details of any renown won (or lost) by your character, for our easy reference. Leave it alone for now.]<br /> <br /> Experience<br /> Saved: 0<br /> Spent: 0<br /> Total: 0<br /> <br /> Freebies Spent<br /> 21 Total<br /> <br /> -1 for totem 2<br /> -2 for empathy 1<br /> -2 for empathy 2<br /> -2 for law 2<br /> -2 for subterfuge 3<br /> -5 for manipulation 3<br /> -1 for computer aptitude<br /> -2 for languages (english, hindi. tamil is his native language)<br /> -2 for supporter<br /> -2 for empathy 3<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6642-abhimanyu","name":"Abhimanyu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6642_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T21:16:55-07:00","id":595347,"title":"","content":"I like the concept Abhi, but I think he needs a name : p Unless I've missed it somehow? I have a few questions though:<br /> <br /> 1. Who did he kill and where? Why was your character around these guys, and why was his First Change triggered in their presence? SF has some pretty dodgy areas, so I suppose a triple homicide wouldn't cause absolute hysteria, but it would probably be front page news. Did someone cover it up (maybe Diego) and if so, does your character owe them? <br /> <br /> 2. Philodox works, but looking at your character's interest in knowledge and the like, theurge might be better. The reason I say this as, although he has a judge demeanor, I'm not really seeing that in his background, or personality, which I'm assuming you're gonna expand on. However, feel free to keep philodox, but I only suggested it as an option. If you all really wanted to be ahrouns or whatever, that's perfectly fine, my only requirement is it makes sense for your character. <br /> <br /> 3. I like the fact he's already helping the Glass Walkers undermine Mistwatch. I'm guessing this is how he's repaying his escape attempt. But why would the Glass Walkers want to prevent his escape? The garou generally aren't presented as a brainwashed cult, where it's loyalty or death. That's closer to the Black Spiral Dancers. So how did the escape attempt fail? If he'd made it back to India, the Glass Walkers probably couldn't have done much. Is there a reason they consider him so valuable? Also, does he resent the Glass Walkers for forcing their will on him? (much like his parents.) <br /> <br /> 4. Resources 4 is a crap tonne of money. I'm assuming it's courtesy of his wealthy parents. But if he's disobeyed them, why do they continue to finance his exploits? They may decide to cut him off...<br /> <br /> 5. As a star sign idea, perhaps Shantar? She favors philodox who are perceived as having great potential. If a Glass Walker theurge believed your character has been blessed by Shantar, they might have thought him essential in their effort to take Mistwatch, and thus, would be unusually insistent in keeping him in San Francisco, Just an idea. You can read about her here: <a href=\"http://darkshadows.awardspace.com/shifters/calendar.htm\" target=\"_blank\">http://darkshadows.awardspace.com/shifters/calendar.htm</a> And I can post her section from Rage Across the Heavens if you like. <br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Eve, I think that's a great cover story. And you're right, no one will believe it, but they'll all insist they do. Garou are funny like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3869-al-haleem","name":"Al-Haleem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3869_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}